Sampling to get concentric rings that then I can then line up again

Oh man, would have saved myself a LOT of time actually reading the documentation carefully and not auto-piloting

Lessons Learned:
1. Mask only works with p5.Image
2. You convert a p5.Graphic to a p5.Image with img = whateverYourGraphicIsCalled.get()
3. Mask uses the ALPHA channel and doesn't depend on colour at all (unlike alpha maps in THREE.js)
p5.Graphics are fully transparent by default, so whatever you draw to the graphic buffer will be the shape of what is retained in the masked image

